h></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></td>\n<td width=\"250\" style=\"text-align:left; border: hidden; padding: 0;\">\n\n<table rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" style=\"border:hidden; border-color:black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 0mm; margin-top: 0mm\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td style=\"border: hidden\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n</td>\n\n</tr>\n</tbody></table><p></p>\n<p>Notice that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"39\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>3</mn></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> (the number of hundreds in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"40\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>3</mn></mstyle></mrow><mn>36</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>) is less than the divisor <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"41\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:</p>\n<p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><table rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"center\" style=\"border:hidden; border-color:black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"150\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0;\">\n\n<table rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" style=\"border:hidden; border-color:black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 0mm; margin-top: 0mm\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"15\" height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0;\"></td>\n<td width=\"15\" height=\"20\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0;\"></td>\n<td width=\"15\" height=\"20\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0;\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"42\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>4</mn></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n<td width=\"15\" height=\"20\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0;\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" style=\"text-align:center; border: hidden; padding: 0\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"43\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-h