    "q-134040": {
      "dom_id": "question-134040",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "After Rose takes her share of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nthan the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\frac{7}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Mark has $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ liters of strawberry juice and $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice remaining.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 4=20.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}=\\frac{13\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{52}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{7}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{52}{20}$ and $\\frac{35}{20}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $52>35,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{52}{20}>\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n\"After Rose takes her part of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is $>$ than the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}>\\frac{7}{4}.$\"",
